  {
   "sha": "1d97599f8b2f4ea6be0b7082ac1d9d93c8d00665",
   "commit": {
    "author": {
     "name": "Doug Patti",
     "date": "2014-01-02T18:05:23Z"
    },
    "committer": {
     "name": "Jonathan Ong",
     "date": "2014-01-14T04:46:07Z"
    },
    "message": "prevent incorrect automatic OPTIONS responses\n\nThe router has automatic handling of OPTIONS based on the registered\nroutes, but if you make an OPTIONS request for an endpoint that does\nnot exist, then it will still return a 200 with nothing allowed.\nInstead, we can let the request move on down the middleware chain. This\nhas two benefits: first, if the route was not defined and no other\nmiddleware handles it, it will return with a 404. Secondly, if multiple\nrouters are used and a later one has the route or a custom OPTIONS\ndefined, the first router will not respond incorrectly."
   },
   "author": {
    "login": "dpatti"
   },
   "html_url": "https://github.com/expressjs/express/commit/1d97599f8b2f4ea6be0b7082ac1d9d93c8d00665"
  },
